{
  "id": "aero-bev",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "name": "Efficient Electric Sedan",
  "description": "Efficient electric sedan sized after the 2022 Tesla Model 3 RWD, to answer one question: what does low drag buy you? Test mass 1,928 kg and road load (EPA's coefficients A/B/C, which hold the axle's drag) from EPA's 2022 Test Car List, 192 kW rated power (EPA), a 9.0 reduction gear (from EPA's N/V), 54 kWh battery (FASTSim's file, no source given). Same layout as the Battery Electric Car, with its motor maps scaled to 192 kW, so the difference between the two is mostly the road load: compare their WLTC runs.\nWhat to expect (lab values, before EPA's label adjustment):\n• EPA city (UDDS): 11.1 kWh/100 km at the socket, 190 MPGe (EPA's test of this car: 185.3 MPGe)\n• EPA highway (HWFET): 12.9 kWh/100 km at the socket, 163 MPGe (EPA: 170.1 MPGe)\n• WLTC Class 3b: 11.8 kWh/100 km at the battery, against the Battery Electric Car's 14.1",
